Bundled Breeze subset for Litterbox named icons.

Source: /usr/share/icons/breeze (Debian package breeze-icon-theme).
License: see LICENSE.breeze (Debian copyright format; upstream LGPL-3.0-or-later).

Included named icons (the theme selects the nearest bundled size):
actions: list-add, application-menu, dialog-ok, mail-mark-read-symbolic,
  overflow-menu, document-open, document-preview, document-edit,
  appointment-new, pin, list-remove, mail-receive, view-refresh,
  transform-move, arrow-right, arrow-down, go-previous, mail-archive,
  dialog-messages, configure, edit-find
places: user-identity, folder
status: system-software-update

Reader/navigation additions use the unmodified Breeze actions/24 SVGs. The
application's mail-archive name maps to Breeze archive-insert-directory.svg
(also shipped upstream as project_archive.svg); Breeze has no mail-archive.svg.
The single 24px source scales for the theme's other requested sizes. Keeping
these names in the bundled theme makes reader, menu and drawer glyphs available
on Android without a system icon theme. The reader pixel-proof target embeds
this same theme and selects it explicitly, so host icons cannot mask omissions.
